        "created_at": "2025-07-17T05:38:47.74255+00:00",
        "notes": "To be clear on how [Sleep Regimen](item_28934e4f-0668-482e-b10d-a5d557cc3b1e)'s mechanics work:\n1. You keep this health throughout every round, it just keeps stacking up\n2. It counts *every sleep you've gotten in the game so far*, so if you've slept 10 total enemies in the first four rounds, you'll get 150 extra health immediately. \nBecause of this, this is a very good power, and what makes you reach 600+ HP in the late rounds. \nBut, if you truly have not hit basically any sleeps so far, and don't think you will be, then [My Turn](item_5cea2ccb-c889-4447-8a84-c704c1da1521) is also a good power to add to your survivability and lethality, especially since now it lasts the entire duration of nano.\n\n [Nebula Conduit](item_476b7040-54c9-4f0c-8283-b4407f6809f8) mixed with [Lumerico Fusion Drive](item_3da81000-333c-460a-a1a2-09441bfda9c8) or nading yourself just adds even more to your level of \"hard to kill\", not even taking your other support healing you into account.\nSee other optional items below if you want more good choices. \n\n[Target Tracker](item_450e11f9-34b6-40c6-b810-0a9ad6c7a093) mixed with [Cluster Core](item_c63cd7ba-b71c-4503-bdb6-4ef0b0a4bdbb) and [Home Remedy](item_de68ba66-26d5-4136-a0c1-6396d3f1b0c7) is actually pretty good, though I only really get it for the increased nade duration, that extra time to kill an enemy or heal a teammate can come in clutch. Other optional items are there if you'd like something else, though.",
